## Report

**Bug (file, line, code)** — `/echo/bind.go`, lines 127–133 (pre-fix), inside `DefaultBinder.bindData`:

```go
	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
		return nil
	}
```

Two defects:
1. It always inserts `v[0]` (a `string`) as the map value, so any map whose element type is not `string`/`interface{}` panics: `reflect.Value.SetMapIndex: value of type string is not assignable to type []string` (confirmed at bind.go:130). `map[string][]string` was therefore unusable.
2. It never initializes a nil destination map, so binding into a nil `map[string]...` panics with "assignment to entry in nil map". It also assumed the key type is `string`.

**Reproduction (before fix)** — throwaway in-package test `/echo/zz_tmp_repro_test.go` (since `bindData` is unexported), calling `b.bindData(&map[string][]string{}, map[string][]string{"foo": {"bar"}}, "form")`:

```
--- FAIL: TestZZTmpBindDataToMap (0.00s)
    --- FAIL: TestZZTmpBindDataToMap/ok,_bind_to_map[string][]string (0.00s)
panic: reflect.Value.SetMapIndex: value of type string is not assignable to type []string [recovered]
	... github.com/labstack/echo/v4.(*DefaultBinder).bindData(...) /echo/bind.go:130
FAIL	github.com/labstack/echo/v4	0.009s
```
(The subtest name matches the reported failing name `ok,_bind_to_map[string][]string`.)

**Fix applied** (`git diff bind.go`):

```diff
 	// Map
-	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
+	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map && typ.Key().Kind() == reflect.String {
+		elemKind := typ.Elem().Kind()
+		isElemString := elemKind == reflect.String
+		isElemSliceOfStrings := elemKind == reflect.Slice && typ.Elem().Elem().Kind() == reflect.String
+		isElemInterface := elemKind == reflect.Interface
+		if !(isElemString || isElemSliceOfStrings || isElemInterface) {
+			// unsupported map value type, nothing to bind
+			return nil
+		}
+		if val.IsNil() {
+			val.Set(reflect.MakeMap(typ))
+		}
 		for k, v := range data {
-			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
+			if isElemSliceOfStrings {
+				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v))
+			} else {
+				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
+			}
 		}
 		return nil
 	}
```

Behaviour: `map[string][]string` gets the full value slice; `map[string]string` / `map[string]interface{}` keep binding the first value (unchanged, no regression); nil maps are allocated; non-string-keyed or unsupported-element maps fall through to the existing `"binding element must be a struct"` path (upstream-consistent); non-map non-struct destinations still error.

